WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:01.802
Euclid's Elements.

2
00:00:01.802 --> 00:00:03.797
Book One, Proposition One.

3
00:00:03.797 --> 00:00:05.870
Given a finite segment A B,

4
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:10.190
construct an equilateral triangle A B C upon it.

5
00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:15.040
With center A and radius A B, describe circle A B.

6
00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:19.720
With center B and radius B A, describe circle B A.

7
00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:22.960
Mark point C where the two circles intersect,

8
00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:26.160
and join segments C A and C B.

9
00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:32.540
Since A is the center of circle A B, segment A C equals segment A B.

10
00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:38.120
Since B is the center of circle B A, segment B C also equals segment B A.

11
00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:45.180
Things equal to the same thing are equal to one another, so A C, A B, and B C are all equal.

12
00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:51.620
Therefore triangle A B C is equilateral, constructed on the given segment A B, as was required to do.
